cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "matrepair — Materiality-Bounded Repair Safety"
message: "If you use this software or benchmark, please cite the accompanying paper."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Prateek
    family-names: Bhatnagar
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-0359-3268"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Prateek2690/matrepair"
abstract: >-
  A reusable benchmark and reference implementation for materiality-bounded,
  reconciliation-preserving repair safety in the automated correction of
  regulated financial figures. Provides a synthetic regulatory-aggregate
  generator, fault injection with ground truth known by construction, a
  deterministic verification gate with a completeness guarantee, and three
  scoring axes not measured by existing repair benchmarks.
keywords:
  - regulatory reporting
  - materiality
  - model risk management
  - expected credit loss
  - automated data repair
  - data quality
  - safety guarantee
  - human-in-the-loop escalation
  - LLM agents
  - trustworthy AI in finance
